{% comment %}
  This section is only to be called by the Section Rendering API.

  `section-rendering-product-card` cannot serve this: it renders a stripped card - variant JSON,
  swatches, price, sku - and no blocks at all, so the subscribe panel is never in its output.
  Rendering the whole product page instead would ship the entire template to update one control.

  The point of fetching rather than computing is that the selling plans a variant actually carries
  are a Liquid question. `variant.selling_plan_allocations` is per variant: a product can hold a
  plan for 200g that 1kg was never allocated, so a panel rendered for one size and left in place
  offers plans the other size cannot be bought on. Requesting this section with `?variant=` makes
  the server answer that question for the size in hand, which is the same answer the product page
  would give.

  Deliberately only `purchase-options`. The variant dropdown beside it lists every variant and does
  not change with the selection, so morphing it would throw away the shopper's open panel and focus
  for no new information.

  The ids are placeholders. A section rendered through this API cannot be told the calling block's
  id, and `purchase-options` uses one to scope `data-purchase-options-id` and the `form` attribute
  that reaches the add to cart form. `variant-select.js` rewrites both onto the fetched markup
  before it morphs, so the panel keeps pointing at its own form.
{% endcomment %}

{% liquid
  if product == blank
    assign product = closest.product
  endif
%}

{% render 'purchase-options',
  product: product,
  form_id: 'card-subscribe-form-placeholder',
  unique_id: 'card-subscribe-panel-placeholder',
  subscription_only: true
%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:names.subscribe_panel_rendering",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "product",
      "id": "product",
      "label": "t:settings.product"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
